---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are chilli flakes?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Chilli flakes (crushed red pepper) are dried chillies crushed into coarse pieces — typically 20–40 mesh — with visible seeds and skin. They sit in the 10,000–20,000 SHU band and are used for pizza topping, seasoning blends and snacks."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What heat level are chilli flakes?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Most chilli flakes are medium heat, 10,000–20,000 SHU, from varieties like Xian pepper, Jinta and Erjingtiao. Higher-heat flakes are available by specifying a hotter variety, but the standard commercial flake is medium."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What mesh size are chilli flakes?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Chilli flakes are a coarse 20–40 mesh — larger than powder (60–80 mesh) but smaller than whole chillies. The coarser cut keeps the seeds and skin visible and gives the flake its characteristic texture."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Chilli Flakes (Crushed Red Pepper) | Tenda Peppers"
  description="China chilli flakes manufacturer — crushed red pepper flakes at 10,000–20,000 SHU, 20–40 mesh, from Xian, Jinta and Erjingtiao. ISO 9001 & HACCP. Tenda Peppers."
  jsonLd={[faqJsonLd]}
>
  <div class="container section">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="font-size:0.9rem;color:#6b5a54;margin-bottom:16px;">
      <a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/products/dried-chillies/">Dried Chillies</a> &rsaquo; Chilli Flakes
    </nav>
    <h1>Chilli Flakes (Crushed Red Pepper)</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Coarse-crushed dried chillies — 20–40 mesh, 10,000–20,000 SHU — the standard form for pizza
      topping, seasoning blends and snack seasoning, milled from Xian, Jinta and Erjingtiao.
    </p>

    <div class="takeaways">
      <strong>Short answer:</strong> Chilli flakes are crushed chilli at 20–40 mesh — coarse enough to stay visible, fine enough to release heat evenly. They sit in the 10,000–20,000 SHU band because flakes are used for <em>everyday</em> heat (pizza, blends, snacks), not extreme heat.
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">What are chilli flakes?</h2>
    <p>
      Chilli flakes, also called crushed red pepper, are dried chillies crushed into coarse pieces with
      visible seeds and skin. They sit at a medium heat (10,000–20,000 SHU) and give dishes both heat
      and a visible, textured finish. The coarser cut is what separates them from powder — see our
      <a href="/specs/mesh-size/">mesh size guide</a> for the full comparison.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Variety</th><th>Heat (SHU)</th><th>Region</th><th>Best for</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Xian pepper</strong></td><td>10,000 – 20,000</td><td>Henan</td><td>Seasoning blends, pizza</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Jinta</strong></td><td>10,000 – 20,000</td><td>Gansu, Xinjiang</td><td>Visible flake, colour</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Erjingtiao</strong></td><td>10,000 – 20,000</td><td>Sichuan</td><td>Aromatic flake, chilli oil</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">What are chilli flakes used for?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Pizza and pasta topping</li>
      <li>Seasoning and spice blends</li>
      <li>Snack and instant-noodle seasoning</li>
      <li>Chilli oil and infused flakes</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">How to specify chilli flakes</h2>
    <p>
      Name the mesh (20–40 is standard), the SHU window and the variety. If you need visible colour,
      Jinta gives a brighter red; Erjingtiao adds aroma without extreme heat. Confirm moisture (under
      13%) and whether you need de-seeded flake — most flake keeps its seeds for texture.
    </p>
    <p class="data-note">
      Heat values are representative per variety. Confirm your exact SHU window, mesh and moisture
      when you inquire.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What are chilli flakes?</h3>
      <p>Chilli flakes (crushed red pepper) are dried chillies crushed into coarse pieces — typically 20–40 mesh — with visible seeds and skin. They sit in the 10,000–20,000 SHU band and are used for pizza topping, seasoning blends and snacks.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What heat level are chilli flakes?</h3>
      <p>Most chilli flakes are medium heat, 10,000–20,000 SHU, from varieties like Xian pepper, Jinta and Erjingtiao. Higher-heat flakes are available by specifying a hotter variety, but the standard commercial flake is medium.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What mesh size are chilli flakes?</h3>
      <p>Chilli flakes are a coarse 20–40 mesh — larger than powder (60–80 mesh) but smaller than whole chillies. The coarser cut keeps the seeds and skin visible and gives the flake its characteristic texture.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:32px;">
      <a class="cta" href="/contact/">Request Flakes Quotation</a>
      <a class="cta cta-outline" href="/products/dried-chillies/chilli-powder/" style="margin-left:8px;">Chilli Powder →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
